ociation":"CONTRIBUTOR","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"- I search through the vcpkg.cpp code.\r\n- I did not see a vcpkg documentation md file updated with the PR/commit\r\n- Prior to commit of this PR https://github.com/microsoft/vcpkg/commit/8414e15973097e70fe40149e922c402799804b3d [vcpkg] Use a tag file rather than conditional compilation to permanently disable metrics. (#15470)\r\n   - One could bootstrap vcpkg with option `-disableMetrics` or set the environment variable  `VCPKG_DISABLE_METRICS=true` and all was fine.\r\n   - Now no matter what `vcpkg` command I put in the message: `Warning: passed --sendmetrics, but metrics are disabled.` appears.\r\n  - The only way I can find to stop the message is to add the command line option `--no-sendmetrics` which is unfriendly user experience method as you have to type it in on every command issuance of `vcpkg`.\r\n- I am asking, is there another way to disable the message with every issuance of `vcpkg` on the command line?\r\n- Otherwise there will need to be more customization to comment out these lines in `vcpkg.cpp`:\r\nhttps://github.com/microsoft/vcpkg/blob/4783c36f8c04f584ec4d232958afae9d32bc61d5/toolsrc/src/vcpkg.cpp#L259-L262\r\n","closed_by":{"login":"BillyONeal","id":1544943,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1NDQ5NDM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1544943?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BillyONeal","html_url":"https://github.com/BillyONeal","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BillyONeal/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BillyONeal/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BillyONeal/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BillyONeal/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BillyON